        "pc_requirements": {
          "minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 7/8/10/11 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i3 or AMD FX-6300<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA GTX 750 Ti / AMD Radeon R7 260X<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 600 MB available space<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Tested on old family PC (broken CPU fan port) with OS Windows 10, CPU Intel Core i7-3770, RAM DDR3 8GB, GPU AMD Radeon HD 5450, game installed on HDD, graphic setting medium. Result: game is laggy but kinda still playable up to stage 2-1, with total RAM used between 3.9GB and 4GB, CPU Load about 10-18%, GPU Load unknown.</li></ul>",
          "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 7/8/10/11 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i7 6700HQ or AMD Ryzen 7 3750H or higher<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 8 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA GTX 950M / AMD Radeon Radeon R7 M375 or higher<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 600 MB available space<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> With this specs, the game should be playable smoothly, even if the game is installed on HDD and graphic setting is set on High.</li></ul>"
